==========================================================================
T2. Is the debut rate higher just after the line than just before it?
==========================================================================
Rate ratio = debuts per club-day in the free zone / in the costly zone.
A club that manages the clock promotes in the free zone, so the clock
predicts a ratio above 1 and a JUMP at the line, not a slope.

  debut clock                costly  443/ 230d = 1.926/d   free  351/ 280d = 1.254/d   ratio 0.651  p=0.0000
  roster-add clock           costly  155/ 208d = 0.745/d   free  308/ 252d = 1.222/d   ratio 1.640  p=0.0000

==========================================================================
T3. Placebo — the identical test at dates with no service consequence
==========================================================================
The same zones, the same widths, slid along the calendar. If the line
carries a clock, the ratio at shift 0 stands out from its neighbours. If
it does not, what the test found is a seasonal promotion rhythm.

  shift   0 (THE LINE)  ratio 0.651  p=0.0000
  shift  10               ratio 1.025  p=0.7830
  shift  20               ratio 0.811  p=0.0085
  shift  30               ratio 1.135  p=0.1306
  shift  35               ratio 1.141  p=0.1069
  shift  40               ratio 1.192  p=0.0281
  shift  50               ratio 0.928  p=0.3466
  shift  60               ratio 0.911  p=0.2497

  placebo shifts run: 76
  placebo ratio median 0.973, min 0.425, max 1.309
  placebo shifts whose ratio EQUALS OR BEATS the real line: 70 of 76  -> permutation p = 0.9221

==========================================================================
T4. Rank-matched controls, and the contrast that matters
==========================================================================
The clock is only worth managing for a man the club expects to hold for
six years. A seasonal rhythm moves everyone. So the sharpest test is not
the pooled ratio — it is whether the ratio is LARGER for the men the
incentive reaches than for the men it does not.

  round 1 pick             n  539  costly  49  free  34  ratio 0.553  p=0.0079
  rounds 2-5               n  676  costly  59  free  48  ratio 0.649  p=0.0318
  round 6+ / undrafted     n 1705  costly 170  free 116  ratio 0.544  p=0.0000
  age at debut <= 23       n  646  costly  48  free  39  ratio 0.648  p=0.0515
  age at debut 24-26       n 1689  costly 143  free 126  ratio 0.703  p=0.0039
  age at debut 27+         n  585  costly  87  free  33  ratio 0.303  p=0.0000
  award tier A or B        n  727  costly  50  free  60  ratio 0.957  p=0.8481
  award tier C or none     n 2193  costly 228  free 138  ratio 0.483  p=0.0000

  INCENTIVE PRESENT        n  794  costly  59  free  51  ratio 0.689  p=0.0549
  INCENTIVE ABSENT         n  307  costly  50  free  10  ratio 0.160  p=0.0000
  free-zone share: incentive present 46.4% vs absent 16.7%  z=3.86 p=0.0001

==========================================================================
T5. Club fixed effects
==========================================================================
Stratified by club: within each club, compare the men it promoted in the
free zone against the men it promoted in the costly zone, against the
club's own exposure. Summing observed - expected across clubs removes
every between-club difference in how often a club promotes at all.

  all debuts     clubs 30  observed in free zone 308  expected 250.2  z=5.39  p=0.0000
  incentive grp  clubs 26  observed in free zone 41  expected 32.5  z=2.23  p=0.0257

